### Summary

I found nothing to flag in either file. In `apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/index.ts`, `notifyOverridesChanged()` now runs in `afterCommit` instead of inside `persistActive`. It therefore runs after `dropPendingCaptures` and `gate.commit`, and a failed persist no longer notifies. The only side effect is that a relocation of the active workspace also calls it, and that is a no-op when nothing changed. In the design spec, the three Part 3 settings rows were above the table header and now sit inside the table. None of the open threads are on these two files, so I added no thread replies.

